    "finite_closed_case": {
      "result": "PASS",
      "construction": "The augmented complex K^p(R,F)=product over (p+1)-fold intersections of closed direct images is stalkwise the contractible simplex complex. For a finite covering the product is finite, and derived global sections of each closed direct image are the cohomology of the closed intersection. The hypercohomology spectral sequence therefore has the required E1 page and abuts to H*(A,F)."
    },
    "paracompact_locally_finite_closed_case": {
      "result": "PASS",
      "construction": "Local finiteness makes the covering-resolution products exact on stalks. On a paracompact space a flasque resolution is soft; its restrictions to closed intersections are soft, and the locally finite products of their closed direct images are soft. These terms are global-section acyclic, so the same E1 page and abutment follow."
    },
